## Alex Masella, President

Alex has collected coins since he was ten. He worked at Numismatic Guaranty Company (NGC) as a grader and numismatist for over a decade, starting while he was still in high school, and directed its tokens and medals department: research, grading, attribution and authentication of rare coins, tokens and medals.

While at NGC he wrote monthly columns for its newsletter and made high-resolution videos of rare coins. He has given talks to coin clubs and attended the ANA Summer Seminar, twice as a young collector and again as an adult.

He holds an AS in Digital Cinema from State College of Florida and a BA in Professional and Technical Communication, with a minor in Business Administration, from the University of South Florida.

## Why Provident

Provident started as a passion project: a holder and label with artistic flair, built around classical and historical themes. Labels can suit a casual collector, an enthusiast or a historian, and the holder is meant to complete the coin it protects.

Beyond grading, the company offers consultation, imaging, attribution and label design, and works with coin shops and auction houses that want to present coins in an attractive, reliable holder.

## What we stand for

- **Innovation** in how a graded coin is presented.
- **Preservation**: every coin is sealed in a tamper-evident holder.
- **Excellence**: careful, consistent work on every coin, whatever its value.

